WEBVTT

00:00:02.440 --> 00:00:06.650
<b>GUNDAM
VICTORY
MOBILE SUIT</b>

00:00:06.650 --> 00:00:12.610
The furious rain, Makes my heart shake
hageshii ame ga, kokoro wo yuruwaseru

00:00:12.610 --> 00:00:15.820
Like it did on that day
Ano hi no youni

00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:22.910
But I just ran through, In my dream I had till yesterday
Tada hashirinuketa, kinou made no MY DREAM

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:26.710
...I still believe
...shinjiteiru no sa

00:00:29.550 --> 00:00:34.470
I'm willing to fight, An endless defense
Owari no nai, defense demo ii yo

00:00:35.090 --> 00:00:42.350
As long as you, Keep on gazing at me
Kimi ga boku wo, mitsumetsuzukete kureru nara

00:00:42.730 --> 00:00:45.270
STAND UP TO THE VICTORY!

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:50.980
Turn to face all the mornings ahead, And someday
Ikutsumono asa wo mukae, Itsuka kitto

00:00:52.070 --> 00:00:53.860
Try to seize them
tsukande miseru

00:00:53.990 --> 00:00:56.450
STAND UP TO THE VICTORY!

00:00:56.780 --> 00:01:02.120
Even if nothing, Lies on the other side
Sono mukougawa ni, nanimonakutemo

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:06.040
It doesn't matter to me
kamawanai kara

00:01:06.210 --> 00:01:14.050
...Just as long as I can embrace, Your gentle, irreplaceable smile!
Kakegae no nai, kimi no yasashii egao daite

00:01:24.500 --> 00:01:28.360
Mankind, having polluted the whole of Earth,

00:01:29.330 --> 00:01:32.560
even after ushering in an era of space colonization,

00:01:32.600 --> 00:01:37.730
just as it had on Earth, repeated its history of war.

00:01:40.430 --> 00:01:45.600
Some wanted to believe it was caused by their instincts...

00:01:45.630 --> 00:01:49.130
...as they tried to adapt to a new environment.

00:01:49.760 --> 00:01:52.130
THE DAY HE MET THE MACHINE

00:01:52.130 --> 00:01:53.730
"The Day He Met The Machine".

00:01:53.730 --> 00:01:54.260
THE DAY HE MET THE MACHINE

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:03.460
Üso fought a mobile suit from BESPA's Yellow Jacket team...

00:02:03.500 --> 00:02:06.900
...with the white mobile suit of the League Militaire.

00:02:10.660 --> 00:02:12.930
If they make you pilot that thing,

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:15.500
then you won't be able to wait in Kasarelia...

00:02:15.530 --> 00:02:19.260
...for your father and mother to return, Üso.

00:02:19.460 --> 00:02:21.830
This machine isn't complete?

00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:27.160
Until three days ago, we were living quietly in Kasarelia.

00:03:04.460 --> 00:03:05.760
What the hell?!

00:03:05.960 --> 00:03:06.600
Haro!

00:03:26.230 --> 00:03:27.060
What?!

00:03:39.630 --> 00:03:41.130
A... A mobile suit?

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:57.330
I'm losing thrust, and my joint core's busted!

00:04:01.130 --> 00:04:02.230
Gotcha!

00:04:07.060 --> 00:04:09.260
Why are you stopping me, Ltjg. Cronicle?

00:04:12.630 --> 00:04:14.930
You're trying to capture it?

00:04:21.330 --> 00:04:22.560
They didn't shoot her down.

00:04:22.600 --> 00:04:24.600
Marbet doesn't die easily.

00:04:24.960 --> 00:04:26.900
She's flying that plane pretty well, huh?

00:04:27.060 --> 00:04:31.200
Who'd have thought we'd run into BESPA's Yellow Jackets here?

00:04:31.660 --> 00:04:34.660
I don't see that paraglider anywhere now.

00:04:34.700 --> 00:04:35.400
Romero!

00:04:35.430 --> 00:04:36.230
Yeah?

00:04:36.260 --> 00:04:40.730
We've set up a few weapons here, could you go get Marbet?

00:04:40.960 --> 00:04:43.930
I dunno, she's got her hands full just trying to escape.

00:04:43.960 --> 00:04:45.730
You act like it's not your problem, too!

00:04:45.760 --> 00:04:48.160
Count! Do we send out another plane?

00:04:48.200 --> 00:04:49.730
And who'd pilot it?

00:04:49.760 --> 00:04:51.130
I can go out.

00:04:51.430 --> 00:04:52.660
Don't be ridiculous.

00:04:52.930 --> 00:04:57.500
If our engine specialist gets killed, who'll finish the mobile suits?

00:05:01.160 --> 00:05:02.900
Okay, I can grab him!

00:05:03.430 --> 00:05:05.530
Shahkti! Hide underground!

00:05:16.260 --> 00:05:17.500
You impudent...

00:05:32.900 --> 00:05:33.800
Stop!

00:05:42.860 --> 00:05:45.200
Time to try a live fire test.

00:05:46.500 --> 00:05:47.430
What?!

00:05:51.830 --> 00:05:53.460
What the hell?!

00:06:15.700 --> 00:06:17.930
Here it comes! Ready the beam rifle!

00:06:17.960 --> 00:06:19.700
Don't! Someone's on board!

00:06:19.730 --> 00:06:23.260
Of course there's someone aboard the mobile suit!

00:06:23.300 --> 00:06:24.600
No, riding on the outside!

00:06:24.630 --> 00:06:25.760
What?!

00:06:31.900 --> 00:06:33.900
Why, you... You!

00:06:34.760 --> 00:06:35.730
Ow!

00:06:40.360 --> 00:06:42.260
What do I do? What do I do?!

00:06:43.230 --> 00:06:44.460
Why, you!

00:06:59.760 --> 00:07:02.660
What...? What?! What the hell is...

00:07:03.100 --> 00:07:04.960
Lower the crane!

00:07:20.730 --> 00:07:22.200
I'm not falling off!

00:07:25.800 --> 00:07:28.000
Okay, now I should be able to catch them.

00:07:28.030 --> 00:07:29.330
Who are you?!

00:07:29.460 --> 00:07:31.030
You knew someone was riding on this thing,

00:07:31.060 --> 00:07:32.860
and you just did what you wanted, anyway?!

00:07:32.900 --> 00:07:34.060
You're one to talk!

00:07:34.360 --> 00:07:35.900
What are you even doing here?!

00:07:35.930 --> 00:07:38.400
You dare defy one of BESPA's Yellow Jackets?!

00:07:38.430 --> 00:07:39.830
This is Earth!

00:07:44.160 --> 00:07:48.700
Dammit, one of the joint computers somewhere must have failed.

00:07:49.730 --> 00:07:50.500
What?!

00:07:53.360 --> 00:07:55.660
Why, you... You! What are you talking about?!

00:07:55.700 --> 00:07:56.830
You get out!

00:07:56.860 --> 00:07:59.030
Why, you little... I'll...

00:07:59.060 --> 00:08:00.160
You overblown...

00:08:06.830 --> 00:08:09.430
Spacenoids should stay in space!

00:08:11.830 --> 00:08:14.930
You people have no right to pollute the Earth!

00:08:17.300 --> 00:08:18.700
It makes no sense!

00:08:20.960 --> 00:08:22.960
Spacenoids coming to Earth?!

00:08:24.260 --> 00:08:25.500
What do you mean?!

00:08:26.060 --> 00:08:30.360
Damn it! BESPA should just stay in the space colonies!

00:08:30.400 --> 00:08:32.030
What are you babbling about?!

00:08:35.630 --> 00:08:36.900
You people!

00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:47.200
Why, you! You!

00:08:47.400 --> 00:08:48.600
Fall!!

00:09:41.300 --> 00:09:42.400
What the hell?!

00:09:43.660 --> 00:09:44.760
I'm flying?

00:09:54.560 --> 00:09:56.730
How humiliating.

00:09:57.400 --> 00:10:02.800
I never expected the League Militaire would attack me with a paraglider!

00:10:04.900 --> 00:10:08.200
What's up? Is Ltjg. Cronicle heading back?

00:10:08.830 --> 00:10:10.500
That's weird.

00:10:13.060 --> 00:10:15.700
Even if he is the Queen's younger brother,

00:10:15.730 --> 00:10:17.600
he shouldn't fly like that.

00:10:17.930 --> 00:10:20.060
Okay, the beam rotors are back online.

00:10:26.030 --> 00:10:30.930
Well, if he wants to go back so badly, I guess I'll go too.

00:10:34.000 --> 00:10:36.200
Is he looking for me?

00:10:38.660 --> 00:10:41.900
What should I do? Can't I do anything while it's in auto?

00:10:42.260 --> 00:10:44.300
There's gotta be a manual or something in here.

00:10:46.100 --> 00:10:47.560
Display manual!

00:10:49.330 --> 00:10:50.260
There it is!

00:10:52.400 --> 00:10:53.560
It's Garry!

00:11:00.660 --> 00:11:02.860
If it flew out of the water automatically,

00:11:02.900 --> 00:11:05.430
there must be some system that'll do something for me!

00:11:14.330 --> 00:11:15.960
This activates the air belt!

00:11:16.500 --> 00:11:18.600
Doesn't it have an auto-balancer or something?

00:11:18.630 --> 00:11:19.560
Ground's close!

00:11:20.560 --> 00:11:23.300
To stop this thing... Do I do this?

00:11:27.660 --> 00:11:30.930
If I keep it upright, I should be able to land.

00:11:36.560 --> 00:11:38.300
Where's the beam rotor?

00:11:38.500 --> 00:11:39.660
What do I do?

00:12:15.260 --> 00:12:16.200
Haro!

00:12:20.360 --> 00:12:21.200
Haro!

00:12:25.700 --> 00:12:26.730
You're bleeding.

00:12:26.830 --> 00:12:27.560
Yeah.

00:12:28.060 --> 00:12:29.160
You're hurt bad.

00:12:32.430 --> 00:12:34.330
Are there scissors in here?

00:12:34.560 --> 00:12:35.430
Yeah.

00:12:36.300 --> 00:12:37.330
Your suit...

00:12:38.300 --> 00:12:42.100
I can't see how bad the wound is unless I cut it off.

00:12:42.130 --> 00:12:47.130
Right... I just applied a pain reliever, so could you wait a bit?

00:12:47.500 --> 00:12:48.300
Sure.

00:12:49.430 --> 00:13:01.160
Haro!

00:13:05.160 --> 00:13:06.900
Haro, where's Shahkti?

00:13:06.930 --> 00:13:16.660
Haro!

00:13:17.700 --> 00:13:19.200
The fighter from before.

00:13:32.960 --> 00:13:34.830
Shahkti, let's go home.

00:13:36.300 --> 00:13:39.130
Don't stay here too long. Please.

00:13:39.360 --> 00:13:40.200
Üso...

00:13:45.200 --> 00:13:46.030
Haro!

00:13:56.800 --> 00:13:57.800
Oh, there she is.

00:13:57.830 --> 00:13:58.660
How's is she?

00:13:58.700 --> 00:13:59.700
Count!

00:13:59.730 --> 00:14:03.860
Did you know we'd run into BESPA's Yellow Jackets here?!

00:14:03.900 --> 00:14:05.860
Sorry. Please forgive me.

00:14:05.900 --> 00:14:07.700
We'll deal with it.

00:14:07.900 --> 00:14:09.230
Will you be here for dinner?

00:14:09.260 --> 00:14:11.200
Sure. I'll be right back.

00:14:22.430 --> 00:14:23.260
I'm home!

00:14:23.700 --> 00:14:24.530
Haro!

00:14:33.700 --> 00:14:35.660
How are you, Miss Katejina Loos?

00:14:36.500 --> 00:14:39.060
I did something terrific today.

00:14:39.360 --> 00:14:42.230
It's difficult to explain how it happened,

00:14:42.760 --> 00:14:46.660
but today, I operated a real mobile suit.

00:14:47.900 --> 00:14:50.460
After this experience, I have a feeling...

00:14:51.200 --> 00:14:54.660
...the rumors about the troops of the Zanscare Empire on Side 2...

00:14:54.700 --> 00:14:58.400
...coming to attack Earth might be true.

00:14:59.060 --> 00:15:01.930
I'm really worried about it, and so I'm writing this to you.

00:15:04.630 --> 00:15:06.560
Miss, it's time for dinner.

00:15:16.330 --> 00:15:17.230
Lately...

00:15:17.260 --> 00:15:18.730
It's real ham.

00:15:19.860 --> 00:15:23.630
Guess they ran off when that mess with the mobile suits happened before.

00:15:23.730 --> 00:15:25.630
There's blueberry jam, too!

00:15:25.700 --> 00:15:26.530
Give it here.

00:15:27.430 --> 00:15:28.130
Good, huh?

00:15:28.160 --> 00:15:29.430
Yeah, good.

00:15:31.860 --> 00:15:34.830
That's the last of the ham my mom made!

00:15:34.860 --> 00:15:36.160
I was saving it!

00:15:37.400 --> 00:15:39.960
Well, the lights weren't on, so we figured...

00:15:39.960 --> 00:15:43.560
How can I hide here if I let the light leak outside?

00:15:43.600 --> 00:15:45.630
Illegal Earth immigrant, right?

00:15:45.930 --> 00:15:47.400
Same as you guys.

00:15:47.430 --> 00:15:48.330
Suzy.

00:15:49.760 --> 00:15:51.630
S-Sorry. May I?

00:15:52.230 --> 00:15:52.930
Sure.

00:15:53.360 --> 00:15:55.300
We got chased out of Largaine.

00:15:56.260 --> 00:15:58.230
Take your right hand out of your pocket.

00:15:58.400 --> 00:16:00.530
If you take out a gun, I'll throw this knife.

00:16:05.330 --> 00:16:06.960
Let's handle this peacefully.

00:16:08.400 --> 00:16:09.300
Haro!

00:16:10.800 --> 00:16:13.630
Those are beam rotors. A lot of them!

00:16:14.630 --> 00:16:16.260
What's that sound?

00:16:16.660 --> 00:16:19.000
It sounds like the machines from before.

00:16:19.860 --> 00:16:21.830
Odelo! Don't go!

00:16:21.900 --> 00:16:23.900
It's a squadron of Zolo copters!

00:16:24.260 --> 00:16:26.300
I haven't seen this many in a while!

00:16:26.330 --> 00:16:27.130
Huh?

00:16:47.800 --> 00:16:51.000
They're going to bomb the special zone in Uwig?

00:16:52.030 --> 00:16:54.260
You think Boysen and the others are safe?

00:16:54.300 --> 00:16:58.230
If that's true, then we need to go help.

00:16:58.460 --> 00:17:00.160
I don't believe this!

00:17:00.200 --> 00:17:03.230
They've just started scattering Minovsky particles.

00:17:09.630 --> 00:17:11.160
Speaking of Uwig,

00:17:11.260 --> 00:17:14.160
the old guys on the Camion said they were headed there.

00:17:14.200 --> 00:17:15.860
"Old guys on the Camion?"

00:17:16.530 --> 00:17:19.400
They're making mobile suits to fight the enemy.

00:17:19.960 --> 00:17:21.500
Like the ones that just flew by?

00:17:21.530 --> 00:17:23.100
I'm ready to join them.

00:17:23.600 --> 00:17:26.600
They had a guillotine in Largaine when we were there.

00:17:26.960 --> 00:17:29.530
Seeing that made me want to fight back.

00:17:29.860 --> 00:17:33.460
The guillotines of Zanscare are being used here on Earth, too?!

00:17:33.530 --> 00:17:36.430
The guillotines of Kagatie, BESPA's leader.

00:17:36.500 --> 00:17:38.200
The 'Gatie Guillotines.

00:17:38.400 --> 00:17:41.630
When the metal blade falls, heads roll.

00:17:42.260 --> 00:17:44.800
Even Suzy saw them use it.

00:17:47.760 --> 00:17:48.760
It's starting!

00:17:49.130 --> 00:17:50.730
It's coming from Uwig.

00:17:55.960 --> 00:17:57.760
That's... amazing.

00:18:01.200 --> 00:18:03.560
Miss Katejina isn't safe!

00:18:06.160 --> 00:18:06.800
Üso...

00:18:07.100 --> 00:18:07.800
Haro!

00:18:11.960 --> 00:18:15.600
What's wrong? Huh, Shahkti?

00:18:17.460 --> 00:18:19.230
Now it can't be stopped.

00:18:22.400 --> 00:18:24.500
This wappa's so slow!

00:18:30.700 --> 00:18:41.560
Haro!

00:18:41.700 --> 00:18:43.400
Haro, you trying to stop me?

00:18:43.430 --> 00:18:44.130
Haro!

00:18:44.860 --> 00:18:47.430
Jeez, you're like a fish, aren't you?

00:18:47.630 --> 00:18:48.200
Here.

00:18:53.530 --> 00:18:56.060
Okay, I've gotta do something.

00:19:03.760 --> 00:19:07.300
Okay, I'll jump, then start the beam rotor. Here we go!

00:19:13.830 --> 00:19:15.060
Beam rotor, start!

00:19:24.230 --> 00:19:25.760
That came from close by.

00:19:26.030 --> 00:19:28.760
Yeah, from the other side of the mountain, I think.

00:19:29.660 --> 00:19:30.560
Flanders.

00:19:32.060 --> 00:19:34.030
The Shokew is still operational?!

00:19:36.800 --> 00:19:41.260
As I thought, Ltjg. Cronicle never returned to the base in Largaine.

00:19:42.030 --> 00:19:44.860
And that Shokew is flying so well...

00:19:45.260 --> 00:19:47.730
What are you up to, Lieutenant Junior Grade?

00:19:54.030 --> 00:19:56.930
What? A friendly unit? No! An enemy!

00:19:57.100 --> 00:19:59.060
Beam rifle, attack!

00:20:00.630 --> 00:20:02.900
Lieutenant, have you turned against us?!

00:20:05.230 --> 00:20:09.000
Dammit! The Minovsky particles are too dense! I can't use the radio!

00:20:09.030 --> 00:20:12.130
Lieutenant! Or is someone else piloting it?!

00:20:13.060 --> 00:20:16.960
Here it comes! I gotta aim! Why isn't it working?!

00:20:20.030 --> 00:20:23.360
That's not the lieutenant. Then is it the League Militaire?

00:20:24.200 --> 00:20:26.560
Gotta release the manual controls... Got it!

00:20:26.600 --> 00:20:28.630
I won't let you have that!

00:20:30.900 --> 00:20:32.460
Why, you!

00:20:32.500 --> 00:20:34.330
I'll cut the control lines!

00:20:38.200 --> 00:20:39.560
He dodged me?!

00:20:41.960 --> 00:20:45.430
I can use this as a shield! Stay back! Stay back!

00:20:54.760 --> 00:20:56.030
Don't insult me!

00:20:56.760 --> 00:20:58.400
I'll let it loose on auto!

00:21:02.630 --> 00:21:04.100
Is there a beam saber?

00:21:14.660 --> 00:21:15.700
Did I get him?

00:21:19.330 --> 00:21:20.060
What?!

00:21:22.900 --> 00:21:24.860
You people!

00:21:26.800 --> 00:21:28.430
Oh, no!

00:21:46.460 --> 00:21:51.200
I... I won... But how?

00:21:53.230 --> 00:21:54.860
No, Üso.

00:21:57.160 --> 00:21:58.130
No!

00:21:58.660 --> 00:21:59.760
Miss Katejina!

00:22:07.730 --> 00:22:11.130
Üso changed after that.

00:22:24.060 --> 00:22:29.530
Piercing the sky, Blue lightning
sora wo tsukisasu aoi inazuma

00:22:29.530 --> 00:22:35.320
Staining the earth, With the shadow of greed
daichi o someteku, yokubou no kage

00:22:36.370 --> 00:22:41.460
Once again, when the nightmare, Envelops the Earth
futatabi akumu ga, sekai wo tsutsumu toki

00:22:41.460 --> 00:22:46.790
You hear voices crying out "S.O.S."
"SOS" wo sakebu koe ga kikoeru...

00:22:48.630 --> 00:22:54.130
Let proud hope fill your heart
hokoritakaki kibou wo mune ni

00:22:54.720 --> 00:23:03.100
And stand up! Say a prayer for peace!!
tachiagare! heiwa no inori komete!

00:23:04.100 --> 00:23:05.100
WINNERS FOREVER!

00:23:06.100 --> 00:23:08.980
In every age
itsuno jidai mo

00:23:08.980 --> 00:23:14.570
...People take risks for freedom
hito wa jiyuu wo kakete

00:23:15.000 --> 00:23:17.000
WINNERS FOREVER!

00:23:18.330 --> 00:23:21.240
The battle goes on
tatakai tsuzukeru

00:23:21.240 --> 00:23:25.920
Fighting all alone in solitude
kodoku na made ni hitori...

00:23:32.900 --> 00:23:35.360
What Üso saw upon entering Uwig...

00:23:35.930 --> 00:23:39.160
...was many refugees fleeing a city engulfed in flames.

00:23:40.660 --> 00:23:43.200
And while searching for Miss Katejina,

00:23:43.500 --> 00:23:48.860
his Shokew is attacked by both the resistance and BESPA Zolos.

00:23:49.700 --> 00:23:53.060
Next time, on Mobile Suit Victory Gundam:

00:23:53.230 --> 00:23:54.230
"Üso's Battle".

00:23:54.260 --> 00:23:55.630
Next Episode ÜSO'S BATTLE

00:23:55.630 --> 00:23:56.730
Please watch it!
